draftpaper (0.7.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The compositor draws only when something may have changed. It looked
    again every refresh after an unchanged frame, forever: about 5% of a
    core and the GPU woken 60 times a second with nothing moving. Idle on
    two displays it is now 0.15% of a core and 4 wakeups a second.
  * What the compositor tells the shell is built only when something may
    have changed, not after every frame drawn or retried.
  * The readings ask BlueZ, power-profiles-daemon and NetworkManager over
    D-Bus instead of starting bluetoothctl, busctl and nmcli twice every
    five seconds: 35 ms of a core a run became 6 ms, and about 69,000
    processes a day became none.
  * A schedule's and the graph's window is made when it is called up and
    let go 20 s after it goes: about 20 MB less in the shell.
  * tests/idle.sh checks that an idle desktop draws almost nothing, and
    draftpaper-compositor msg frames counts the frames drawn.
  * docs/sheet-client.md: a plan for the sheet's lettering in a small Rust
    client instead of Quickshell. Nothing built.

