draftpaper (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rulers (#48, Mod+r, `draftpaper rulers`): a horizontal and a vertical
    ruler, frame line to frame line, crossing at a point that slides
    anywhere on the sheet, one piece where they cross; both edges graduated
    in true millimetres, numbered by one (the top, the right), counted from
    each ruler's own sliding zero both ways. The crossing and the zeros move
    1 mm (10 with Shift), a ruler turns 1° (15°), freely or locked at any
    angle; inclined, the degrees show; angles typed in the panel, which
    hides. While they are out the compositor holds the pointer to their
    millimetres at any angle (rulers.rs).
  * A scale bar in the bottom margin (#44), true to size on each screen
    (NTS on a display that reports no size); [title] scale.
  * A revision block above the title block (#45): the focused window's git
    repository's latest commits, `draftpaper revisions`; off by default,
    [title] revisions. git runs with nothing of the repository's own
    configuration able to start a program.
  * Hatching for parked windows' cells (#46), broken around their
    lettering; a theme's [sheet] hatch_strength, hatch_spacing.
  * A key plan with several screens (#47): their outlines as arranged, this
    one filled, the focused one heavier, and a north mark (a square with a
    cross, the arm toward each other screen thick); [title] key_plan.
  * The headless backend drives several outputs (--headless WxH,WxH); IPC:
    "rulers", "pointer", windows' pid; the pointer_by action.
  * make always hands the programs to cargo (a stale build was tested).
  * toml 1.1, png 0.18; screenshots written fast and renamed into place.
  * The website, https://draftpaper.este.systems/, in the README and the
    manual.

