draftpaper (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security (#41): `draftpaper tmux restore` no longer types a saved
    program back when one of its words holds a control character. A file
    name with Ctrl+C and Enter in it, opened in a tmux pane, could run a
    command of its own the next time the tmux server started.
  * The login screen's fingerprint glyph lights up while the reader
    listens: Qt 6.8's curve renderer did not repaint the stroke colour
    changed after the first frame; the glyph is now the ink, faint by its
    opacity.
  * The dependencies are audited against RustSec on every change and
    weekly; SECURITY.md says how to report a vulnerability privately.
  * The README's pictures are new, in Soft Glow, the settings' wallpaper
    page among them.

