draftpaper (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The session comes back after a logout or a reboot (#38): every
    application open at the end starts again at login (its desktop entry,
    else its command line), each window back on its workspace and zones,
    floating, fullscreen or parked in its cell. Saved to
    ~/.local/state/draftpaper/session.json once it has held, and by
    Mod+Shift+e; config.toml [session] restore, skip. Windows put back out
    of sight are sent their first configure, so they draw once shown.
  * The applications as they were left: a terminal starts in its shell's
    directory and runs again what it ran (an editor, a pager, a monitor,
    tmux); an application started with documents opens them again.
    `draftpaper apply` switches on each one's own restore ([session] apps):
    Firefox and Chromium their tabs, Emacs its files at their places
    (desktop-save-mode), Neovim the cursor and a session per directory, tmux
    its sessions across a reboot (`draftpaper tmux save|keep|restore`).
  * A lock screen of Draftpaper's own (`draftpaper lock`, qml/lock.qml, PAM
    service draftpaper-lock) in place of swaylock, which stays a fallback:
    the sheet blurred, nothing of the windows, one field. The login and lock
    screens are one field and no words; the margins stay sharp.
  * The fingerprint reader listens as often as it takes on both screens:
    when pam_fprintd gives up with nothing typed, the conversation starts
    over; a finger not recognised shakes the field.
  * The login screen no longer gets stuck after Escape while the reader
    listens, and recovers when greetd does not start the session.
  * The settings' wallpaper page scrolls through every picture.
  * The compositors' log level is DRAFTPAPER_LOG, no longer RUST_LOG
    exported to the whole session. A better fingerprint glyph (Tabler
    Icons, MIT).

